All 15 files read. The variant is a minimal offline desktop game: no network, no serialization, no digests, no native code, no applet. The single security-relevant surface is the AI-plugin class loader, which I've traced end to end (dialog → class name → `player/<name>.class` bytes → `defineClass` → `newInstance` before any type check), including an analysis of why the dot-to-separator conversion coincidentally blocks `..` traversal.

