  "notes": "This variant is a 15-file, ~2550-line offline Swing desktop game (TutorVolleyMain.java:14 extends JFrame, main() at :96) - by far the simplest member of the corpus examined: NO network code at all (grep for URL/Socket/URLConnection/http/.php/apo-games across all 15 files returns nothing), no highscore or level submission, no save/replay files, no ObjectInputStream, no MessageDigest/MD5, no System.load/loadLibrary, no System.getProperty use, no file writes. The only file-system input in the entire variant is the class loader's FileInputStream plus classpath image loads with hardcoded '/images/...' paths (TutorVolleyImage.java:103, all call sites hardcoded). Path traversal was actively analyzed and rejected as an independent finding: name.replace('.', File.separatorChar) at TutorVolleyClassLoader.java:38 consumes every dot into a separator, so a '..' path segment can never be formed from dialog input, and on Unix new File(root, child) joins an absolute child under the root rather than replacing it; only on Windows would a drive-absolute child (e.g. 'C:\\x') escape the 'player' root, and that actor is the same local user already covered by TutorVolley-01. The class loader's header comment 'Wird hier genutzt, um die Hamster neu zu laden' (used here to reload the hamsters, TutorVolleyClassLoader.java:11) is a stale comment from an unrelated project - direct textual evidence of clone-and-own propagation, supporting shared_component=true for finding 01. Secondary robustness issues subsumed by finding 01 (a loaded plugin already has arbitrary code execution): a malicious AI can hang the game timer thread inside a single think() call since the average-think-time guard at TutorVolleyPlayer.java:208-218 only fires after 40 returned samples, and a plugin returning null from getName() causes NPEs at TutorVolleyPanelGame.java:292/466 via TutorVolleyPlayer.getName():114."
